  "question": {
    "text": "If <math><mi>a</mi></math> and <math><mi>b</mi></math> are two real numbers lying between <math><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><mn>1</mn></math>, such that <math><msub><mrow><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><msub><mrow><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> form an equilateral triangle, then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
